  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 4907.05 Disciplinary Action",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 4907.05 Disciplinary Action.\n\n(a) The commissioner, after a hearing has determined that a certificate holder has committed misconduct, shall impose disciplinary action in any one or more of the following ways:\n\n(1) By reprimand;\n\n(2) By requiring the person to take remedial or corrective actions;\n\n(3) By requiring the person to participate in a program of training in the area or areas in which the certificate holder has been found deficient; or\n\n(4) By suspension of certificate for:\n\na. A period not to exceed 6 months for a first offense within any 5-year period;\n\nb. A period not to exceed 1 year for a second offense within any 5-year period; and\n\nc. A period not to exceed 5 years for a third offense within any 5-year period.\n\n(b) In determining what disciplinary action to impose, the commissioner shall consider the following factors:\n\n(1) Whether the certificate holder has committed any violations in the prior 24 months;\n\n(2) Whether the aggrieved conduct negatively affected or potentially affected the health or safety of others; and\n\n(3) Whether there are any mitigating circumstances or factors.\n\nSource. #8650, eff 6-2-06\n\nAPPENDIX",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c4900.html"
}
